 36S  c  Compiled by J. Chen (FRIB, MSU), September 3, 2022                     
 36S  c  2022Gr07: E=215 MeV (mid-target) {+36}S beam was produced from the     
 36S 2c  Tandem-ALPI accelerator complex at the INFN Legnaro National           
 36S 3c  Laboratory, Italy. Target was 99.7% enriched {+208}Pb with a thickness 
 36S 4c  of 1 mg/cm{+2} on a 1 mg/cm{+2} Nb backing mounted onto the Cologne    
 36S 5c  differential plunger. Fragments were detected and identified with the  
 36S 6c  PRISMA magnetic spectrometer. |g rays were detected with the AGATA     
 36S 7c  Demonstrator array consisting of five triple cluster modules of        
 36S 8c  36-folded segmented Ge crystals. Measured E|g, I|g, fragment-|g-coin,  
 36S 9c  recoil distance. Deduced levels, lifetimes. Comparisons with           
 36S ac  shell-model calculations.                                              
